                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "As someone with a fear of thalassophobia, this game definitely made me wet my pants during the first half. However, after a while, the gameplay became repetitive, and I found myself wanting to just finish the game.\n\nThe water itself was genuinely terrifying, but outside of that, the gameplay mostly felt like swimming from one place to another and triggering events. There was also a section where I couldn't move forward no matter what I tried, which became extremely frustrating and took me out of the experience.\n\nI enjoyed parts of the game, but not as much as other thalassophobia games I've played. There were several moments where I wished the gameplay and ending had been handled differently.\n\nOverall, I'd give Debris, 5.5 out of 10 Debris.\n\nGAMEPLAY\nPART 1 (Game Starts at: 4:10:38): https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qC5BFNbGiEk&t=15s\nPART 2(Game Starts at: 1:23:27): https://youtu.be/vlHzSgH2t5c?si=IJ6X1gcqo3IU-Ltv&t=5007",
